    {
      "v": 3,
      "zh": "他对我说：「这是发出行在遍地上的咒诅。凡偷窃的必按卷上这面的话除灭；凡起假誓的必按卷上那面的话除灭。",
      "en": "The speaker went on to say, “This is a curse[NOTE:1] traveling across the whole earth. For example, according to the curse whoever steals[NOTE:2] will be removed from the community; or on the other hand (according to the curse) whoever swears falsely will suffer the same fate.”",
      "notes": [
        "The Hebrew word translated “curse” (אָלָה, ʾalah) alludes to the covenant sanctions that attend the violation of God’s covenant with Israel (cf. Deut 29:12, 14, 20-21).",
        "Stealing and swearing falsely (mentioned later in this verse) are sins against mankind and God respectively and are thus violations of the two major parts of the Ten Commandments. These two stipulations (commandments 8 and 3) represent the whole law."
      ],
