    {
      "v": 6,
      "zh": "我说：「这是甚么呢？」他说：「这出来的是量器。」他又说：「这是恶人在遍地的形状。」",
      "en": "I asked, “What is it?” And he replied, “It is a basket for measuring grain[NOTE:1] that is moving away from here.” Moreover, he said, “This is their ‘eye’[NOTE:2] throughout all the earth.”",
      "notes": [
        "Heb “[This is] the ephah.” An ephah was a liquid or solid measure of about a bushel (five gallons or just under twenty liters). By metonymy it refers here to a measuring container (probably a basket) of that quantity.",
        "The LXX and Syriac read עֲוֹנָם (ʿavonam, “their iniquity,” so NRSV; NIV similar) for the MT עֵינָם (ʿenam, “their eye”), a reading that is consistent with the identification of the woman in v. 8 as wickedness, but one that is unnecessary. In 4:10 the “eye” represented divine omniscience and power; here it represents the demonic counterfeit."
      ],
